export const sourceCode = "# Introduction\n\n<SdkName /> is a comprehensive React SDK for integrating crypto wallet connection functionality into your applications. It provides a configurable wallet list modal and basic account operations.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe SDK supports two main types of wallets:\n\n- **Social Wallets**: Email-based passwordless wallets and social login wallets (Google, X/Twitter)\n- **EOA Wallets**: External wallet applications (MetaMask, WalletConnect, etc.)\n\nEach wallet type supports different methods and operations, providing flexibility for various use cases.\n\n## Key Features\n\n- **Easy Integration**: Simple setup with React hooks\n- **Multiple Wallet Support**: Connect to various wallet types (EVM, Dogecoin)\n- **Social Login**: Support for email passwordless and social login methods\n- **Theme Customization**: Customize the UI to match your brand\n- **TypeScript Support**: Full TypeScript definitions for better developer experience\n\n## Requirements\n\n- React 18 or higher\n- TypeScript 5 or higher (recommended)\n\n## Installation\n\nInstall the SDK using your preferred package manager:\n\n```bash\n  npm install __PACKAGE_NAME__\n\n```\n\n```bash\n  pnpm add __PACKAGE_NAME__\n\n```\n\n```bash\n  yarn add __PACKAGE_NAME__\n\n```\n\n## Quick Example\n\n```tsx\n  import { WalletConnectProvider, useWalletConnect, useAccount } from \"__PACKAGE_NAME__\";\n\n  function App() {\n    return (\n      <WalletConnectProvider\n        config={{\n          clientId: \"your-client-id\",\n        }}\n      >\n        <WalletDemo />\n      </WalletConnectProvider>\n    );\n  }\n\n  function WalletDemo() {\n    const { openModal, isConnected, disconnect } = useWalletConnect();\n    const { address, chainId, signMessage } = useAccount();\n\n    return (\n      <div>\n        {isConnected ? (\n          <div>\n            <div>Address: {address}</div>\n            <div>Chain ID: {chainId}</div>\n            <button onClick={() => signMessage?.({ message: \"Hello\" })}>\n              Sign Message\n            </button>\n            <button onClick={disconnect}>Disconnect</button>\n          </div>\n        ) : (\n          <button onClick={openModal}>Connect Wallet</button>\n        )}\n      </div>\n    );\n  }\n\n```\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Read the [Quick Start](./quickstart) guide to get started\n- Explore the [Provider Configuration](./provider-config) for advanced setup\n- Check out the [Hooks](./hooks) documentation for available hooks\n- Learn about [Providers](./providers) for chain-specific operations";
